1
00:02:31,193 --> 00:02:37,193
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:37,193 --> 00:02:41,193
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:41,193 --> 00:02:45,193
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:45,193 --> 00:02:50,193
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:50,193 --> 00:02:53,193
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:53,193 --> 00:02:56,193
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:56,193 --> 00:02:59,193
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government

8
00:02:59,193 --> 00:03:02,193
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:04,193 --> 00:03:06,193
Now this is exciting!

10
00:03:06,193 --> 00:03:09,193
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:09,193 --> 00:03:12,193
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:12,193 --> 00:03:17,193
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:20,193 --> 00:03:22,193
Separated from the rest of his crew,

14
00:03:22,193 --> 00:03:26,193
Luffy has finally arrived at Marineford to rescue his brother Ace.

15
00:03:26,193 --> 00:03:29,193
The Whitebeard Pirates have successfully pushed into the Bay,

16
00:03:29,193 --> 00:03:32,193
but a massive number of Marines still block the path to Ace.

17
00:03:32,193 --> 00:03:35,193
The battle is spreading to the Bay Head,

18
00:03:35,193 --> 00:03:40,193
where allies of Whitebeard are under attack from the Navy's human weapons, the Pacifistas.

19
00:03:40,193 --> 00:03:46,193
Oh, Squad, good to see you're alive.

20
00:03:46,193 --> 00:03:48,193
Yeah, barely.

21
00:03:48,193 --> 00:03:51,193
Is that so? I was trying to reach you earlier.

22
00:03:51,193 --> 00:03:54,193
How are things looking at the Bay Head now?

23
00:03:54,193 --> 00:03:58,193
I'm sorry to say, but your allies were beaten pretty badly.

24
00:03:58,193 --> 00:04:01,193
As for me, I only managed to get out of there through sheer luck.

25
00:04:01,193 --> 00:04:04,193
Sengoku is one merciless bastard.

26
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:07,193
He's pulling out every dirty trick he can think of.

27
00:04:07,193 --> 00:04:12,193
Judging by your shift in tactic, I'm guessing you picked up on the Navy's plan.

28
00:04:12,193 --> 00:04:16,193
I've known Sengoku and what he's capable of for a long time.

29
00:04:19,193 --> 00:04:21,193
Huh? What's Squad doing up there?

30
00:04:21,193 --> 00:04:25,193
You have 43 allied captains willing to die for you.

31
00:04:25,193 --> 00:04:29,193
We're all in your debt, for now and for always.

32
00:04:29,193 --> 00:04:33,193
We consider it a privilege to risk our lives for you and your crew.

33
00:04:33,193 --> 00:04:35,193
Huh?

34
00:04:53,193 --> 00:04:56,193
Akainu's plot. Whitebeard entrapped.

35
00:05:04,193 --> 00:05:11,193
Ones of the Deaf

36
00:05:17,193 --> 00:05:21,193
Chilinder

37
00:05:24,193 --> 00:05:26,193
1

38
00:05:26,193 --> 00:05:56,173
Thank you.

39
00:05:56,193 --> 00:06:26,173
Thank you.

40
00:06:26,193 --> 00:06:56,173
Thank you.

41
00:06:56,193 --> 00:07:26,173
Thank you.

42
00:07:26,173 --> 00:07:56,153
Thank you.

43
00:07:56,153 --> 00:07:58,153
Thank you.

44
00:07:58,153 --> 00:08:00,153
Thank you.

45
00:08:00,153 --> 00:08:02,153
Thank you.

46
00:08:02,153 --> 00:08:04,153
Thank you.

47
00:08:04,153 --> 00:08:06,153
Thank you.

48
00:08:06,353 --> 00:08:07,493
Don't move, Pops.

49
00:08:07,653 --> 00:08:09,653
You'll make things worse if you keep squirming.

50
00:08:10,153 --> 00:08:11,053
Whitebeard.

51
00:08:15,153 --> 00:08:16,693
I'm serious.

52
00:08:16,833 --> 00:08:18,093
This battle is a fake.

53
00:08:18,293 --> 00:08:19,133
Just ask him.

54
00:08:19,133 --> 00:08:22,973
I know about your treacherous deal with the Navy.

55
00:08:23,133 --> 00:08:27,553
You have their assurance that Ace and all of your pirates won't even get scratched.

56
00:08:27,913 --> 00:08:29,693
They'll just go after your allies.

57
00:08:32,473 --> 00:08:33,853
Wait, what's he saying?

58
00:08:34,173 --> 00:08:37,293
Is it true that they're just targeting us?

59
00:08:38,013 --> 00:08:40,473
Everybody, listen up!

60
00:08:41,133 --> 00:08:43,133
Whitebeard's been playing us all for fools.

61
00:08:43,133 --> 00:08:48,813
All this time, you've kept it a secret.

62
00:08:49,813 --> 00:08:54,533
You didn't have the guts to tell me that Ace is actually the son of that wretched pirate,

63
00:08:54,933 --> 00:08:55,713
Gold Roger.

64
00:08:55,713 --> 00:09:07,033
When you first found me, I was alone in this world.

65
00:09:07,553 --> 00:09:08,593
A complete wreck.

66
00:09:08,593 --> 00:09:16,873
The sport is out of his mind again.

67
00:09:17,173 --> 00:09:18,713
He's dangerous when he's like this.

68
00:09:18,953 --> 00:09:19,653
Stay away.

69
00:09:19,993 --> 00:09:20,673
Come on.

70
00:09:20,913 --> 00:09:21,533
This again?

71
00:09:21,613 --> 00:09:24,493
Once it starts, you just gotta sit back and ride it out.

72
00:09:29,153 --> 00:09:31,493
Isn't there anyone strong enough to face me?

73
00:09:31,793 --> 00:09:32,693
I'm right here.

74
00:09:32,993 --> 00:09:33,873
Bring it on.

75
00:09:34,493 --> 00:09:35,873
How's about Gold Roger?

76
00:09:36,193 --> 00:09:37,113
Where's he at?

77
00:09:37,113 --> 00:09:39,153
What's the matter?

78
00:09:39,393 --> 00:09:40,573
Are you all scared?

79
00:09:41,693 --> 00:09:43,473
Give me your best shot!

80
00:09:48,433 --> 00:09:51,413
You knew why I was all alone that day.

81
00:09:57,893 --> 00:10:03,673
My precious crew, who had fought alongside me in so many battles, was killed by Gold Roger.

82
00:10:03,673 --> 00:10:10,173
You know this, and you know that I despise Roger, more than anything!

83
00:10:11,033 --> 00:10:17,553
Yet you still kept these secrets from me, that Ace was Roger's son, that you were helping him become the next king of the pirates!

84
00:10:18,033 --> 00:10:19,873
How could I trust someone like you?

85
00:10:19,873 --> 00:10:22,233
Never mind the Whitebeard's son, that's why I'm going to help him become the king of the pirates!

86
00:10:22,233 --> 00:10:24,293
That's why I'm going to help him become the king of the pirates!

87
00:10:24,293 --> 00:10:27,233
The old guy, he wants Ace to be the king?

88
00:10:27,233 --> 00:10:35,113
Because you see, Whitebeard's the greatest pirate I've ever met, that's why I'm going to help him become the king of the pirates!

89
00:10:35,113 --> 00:10:45,733
You've been betraying me, and playing me for a fool since the very beginning!

90
00:10:46,613 --> 00:10:48,173
I didn't have a damn clue!

91
00:10:48,713 --> 00:10:51,773
I bet you laughed your ass off when I became friends with Ace!

92
00:10:52,613 --> 00:10:56,693
Then your favorite son got caught, and you showed your true colors!

93
00:10:57,253 --> 00:11:02,013
All of the Whitebeard pirates are inside the bay, while us Allied pirates are stuck outside!

94
00:11:03,733 --> 00:11:10,073
Forty-three captains fight beside you, and you handed us all to the Navy, just to protect Roger's son!

95
00:11:10,073 --> 00:11:16,113
We Allied pirates will be obliterated, whereas Ace and your men will be completely safe!

96
00:11:16,613 --> 00:11:19,913
That's your underhanded deal with Sengoku, isn't it?

97
00:11:23,493 --> 00:11:26,773
What? Firefist Ace is Roger's son?

98
00:11:26,993 --> 00:11:32,253
That's right, and our superiors already have an agreement regarding how this war is going to end.

99
00:11:32,293 --> 00:11:35,313
Go to hell! I don't believe a word of that crap!

100
00:11:35,773 --> 00:11:37,873
Whether you believe it or not doesn't matter.

101
00:11:37,873 --> 00:11:40,313
You're going to end up dead anyway.

102
00:11:40,433 --> 00:11:43,693
That's enough! We'll see who ends up dead, you wretch!

103
00:11:50,753 --> 00:11:55,533
You're a stubborn brat, but you'll learn what I'm talking about soon enough.

104
00:11:56,093 --> 00:11:57,813
Stand up and look for yourself.

105
00:12:00,753 --> 00:12:07,313
We plan to converge our forces soon, then attack the Allied pirates, only them.

106
00:12:07,873 --> 00:12:12,773
And Whitebeard, the Navy isn't even going to lay a finger on his gang of pirates.

107
00:12:19,233 --> 00:12:25,653
Not one of us knew the truth, and so we followed you, risking our lives to help rescue Ace,

108
00:12:26,093 --> 00:12:30,013
only to find out we were nothing more than sacrificing to you!

109
00:12:30,013 --> 00:12:34,853
We're the ones bearing the brunt of the Navy's attacks!

110
00:12:35,193 --> 00:12:36,373
It's as clear as day!

111
00:12:36,373 --> 00:12:57,593
Those monsters approach from the back, and the ice blocks us on both sides!

112
00:12:57,913 --> 00:12:59,673
There's no way we can escape!

113
00:12:59,673 --> 00:13:04,053
Whitebeard, old buddy!

114
00:13:04,593 --> 00:13:06,053
Is he telling the truth?

115
00:13:06,053 --> 00:13:07,373
He's lying his teeth off!

116
00:13:07,573 --> 00:13:08,333
He's gotta be!

117
00:13:15,513 --> 00:13:18,173
It's a miracle I was able to stab you.

118
00:13:19,653 --> 00:13:21,553
Well, now it's your turn!

119
00:13:22,113 --> 00:13:22,973
Kill me!

120
00:13:22,973 --> 00:13:31,673
The ice wall is in the way!

121
00:13:31,893 --> 00:13:33,453
We're blocked off on every side!

122
00:13:33,493 --> 00:13:33,873
Oh, no!

123
00:13:34,413 --> 00:13:35,213
Is this the end?

124
00:13:36,433 --> 00:13:41,573
He was right!

125
00:13:41,833 --> 00:13:42,233
Look!

126
00:13:42,433 --> 00:13:44,233
The Navy's only going after us!

127
00:13:47,613 --> 00:13:48,313
Run away!

128
00:13:48,313 --> 00:13:48,753
Run away!

129
00:13:48,753 --> 00:13:48,833
Run away!

130
00:13:48,833 --> 00:13:49,333
Run away!

131
00:13:49,333 --> 00:13:49,833
Run away!

132
00:13:49,833 --> 00:13:50,833
Run away!

133
00:13:50,833 --> 00:13:51,833
Run away!

134
00:13:51,833 --> 00:13:52,833
Run away!

135
00:13:53,033 --> 00:13:53,933
Old buddy!

136
00:13:53,933 --> 00:13:56,853
Please tell me we're not throwing our lives away!

137
00:13:56,853 --> 00:13:58,913
Just so you can save us!

138
00:14:00,513 --> 00:14:01,773
Please, say something!

139
00:14:01,773 --> 00:14:02,373
Anything!

140
00:14:02,373 --> 00:14:03,373
Whitebeard!

141
00:14:22,833 --> 00:14:38,973
It can't be true. It's impossible.

142
00:14:39,473 --> 00:14:41,073
Whitebeard wouldn't sell out fellow pirates.

143
00:14:41,273 --> 00:14:42,573
He did that to his allies?

144
00:14:42,713 --> 00:14:44,713
No way. He'd fight the Navy head-on.

145
00:14:45,053 --> 00:14:47,073
Whitebeard and the Navy are in cahoots.

146
00:14:47,253 --> 00:14:50,073
All those New World pirates who trusted and followed Whitebeard.

147
00:14:50,073 --> 00:14:51,713
I know. I can't believe it.

148
00:14:51,713 --> 00:14:54,093
They're all rushing to their doom thanks to his betrayal.

149
00:14:54,453 --> 00:14:55,893
I didn't want to believe it.

150
00:14:56,153 --> 00:14:57,533
We're all sons to you.

151
00:14:57,933 --> 00:15:00,613
But I guess some kids are just worth more than others.

152
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:01,873
You're a damn fool!

153
00:15:02,273 --> 00:15:04,293
The Navy is deceiving you, Squard.

154
00:15:04,453 --> 00:15:06,253
Why trust them instead of Pops?

155
00:15:06,433 --> 00:15:07,693
I know you're in on the deal.

156
00:15:07,853 --> 00:15:09,593
Don't you play dumb with me!

157
00:15:10,393 --> 00:15:12,273
You're the First Division Commander.

158
00:15:12,753 --> 00:15:15,113
You're basically Whitebeard's right-hand man.

159
00:15:15,273 --> 00:15:17,953
If anyone knows about his deal with the Navy, it's you!

160
00:15:17,953 --> 00:15:23,173
It ain't Ace's fault his old man killed Squard's crew, but it is what it is.

161
00:15:23,733 --> 00:15:27,153
And I can only blame myself for keeping it a secret all these years.

162
00:15:27,253 --> 00:15:28,633
The Navy made the right move.

163
00:15:29,413 --> 00:15:32,413
That doesn't make you any less of a bastard, though, Sengoku.

164
00:15:32,913 --> 00:15:35,073
Even if you are a crafty one.

165
00:15:35,813 --> 00:15:37,173
It's time to win this.

166
00:15:37,613 --> 00:15:38,393
Go, Aokiji!

167
00:15:38,393 --> 00:15:41,513
Oh, no!

168
00:15:41,693 --> 00:15:42,753
Don't talk it up!

169
00:15:43,353 --> 00:15:45,073
This entire war is a setup?

170
00:15:45,513 --> 00:15:47,113
It can't seriously be fake.

171
00:15:47,273 --> 00:15:49,333
I've wasted my whole day watching this stuff.

172
00:15:51,693 --> 00:15:52,973
It shut off.

173
00:15:53,113 --> 00:15:53,973
What's wrong?

174
00:15:54,013 --> 00:15:54,713
Is it broken?

175
00:16:05,053 --> 00:16:06,813
Now activate the walls.

176
00:16:06,973 --> 00:16:07,213
Right!

177
00:16:08,393 --> 00:16:22,733
The pirate who defeated me would never be struck down so easily, especially by his own ally.

178
00:16:23,593 --> 00:16:26,553
You're not worth my time anymore, old man!

179
00:16:26,913 --> 00:16:30,553
If this is how the Great Whitebeard dies, you'll make a fool of us both!

180
00:16:30,553 --> 00:16:37,633
Oh, boy, that was harsh.

181
00:16:37,973 --> 00:16:39,673
Then it was a matter of pride.

182
00:16:39,673 --> 00:16:45,333
It's true.

183
00:16:45,333 --> 00:16:49,333
He could have easily blocked that if he was as tough as he used to be.

184
00:16:50,333 --> 00:16:54,993
It wouldn't have mattered that it was a surprise attack, or that it came from one of his allies.

185
00:16:55,993 --> 00:16:59,473
Has Pops gotten weaker than we thought, and I just didn't notice?

186
00:16:59,473 --> 00:17:03,553
I don't want no sympathy.

187
00:17:03,793 --> 00:17:06,453
There's no way I'm wearing this crap in front of my enemies.

188
00:17:06,653 --> 00:17:07,513
What, Pops?

189
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:10,153
He's letting his health get worse and worse.

190
00:17:10,153 --> 00:17:36,013
I don't know if you realize the magnitude of what you've just done.

191
00:17:36,013 --> 00:17:42,953
Squared, you thrust a sword into your father's body trying to kill him.

192
00:17:43,573 --> 00:17:46,933
You've lost your way, my poor stupid son!

193
00:17:46,933 --> 00:18:03,493
But I still love you, even if you are a damn fool.

194
00:18:03,493 --> 00:18:20,433
Cut the crap.

195
00:18:21,033 --> 00:18:22,573
You've sold our lives out.

196
00:18:23,313 --> 00:18:24,093
All of us.

197
00:18:24,493 --> 00:18:31,073
Who took your loyal and steadfast heart away from your father and delivered it into the hands of our enemies?

198
00:18:31,073 --> 00:18:33,033
Now you tell me his name.

199
00:18:34,173 --> 00:18:34,773
Aka'inu.

200
00:18:35,953 --> 00:18:37,293
Admiral Aka'inu.

201
00:18:39,213 --> 00:18:41,993
I'm opposed to such an underhanded plan.

202
00:18:43,093 --> 00:18:46,773
Most people don't know the truth, so they call Whitebeard a hero.

203
00:18:47,613 --> 00:18:51,713
They don't think twice about praising the man, but you know better.

204
00:18:51,713 --> 00:18:57,453
He's a scumbag who came to us with a deal, one that protects his and his pirates' interests,

205
00:18:57,713 --> 00:19:01,553
but betrays his New World allies without so much as a second thought.

206
00:19:02,553 --> 00:19:04,853
All those stories and legends are made up.

207
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:08,653
The one we should kill in this war is Whitebeard.

208
00:19:08,993 --> 00:19:11,693
Letting him live would be a great disservice to the world.

209
00:19:12,533 --> 00:19:16,813
If you can help me, I'll save all of the New World pirates.

210
00:19:19,013 --> 00:19:19,493
Whitebeard.

211
00:19:19,493 --> 00:19:20,633
Kill him.

212
00:19:25,593 --> 00:19:29,953
He said if I killed you, he would save your New World allies.

213
00:19:31,493 --> 00:19:32,053
Aka'inu.

214
00:19:32,333 --> 00:19:33,873
So that's what he told you.

215
00:19:34,433 --> 00:19:37,493
I completely understand how much you hate Gold Roger.

216
00:19:38,293 --> 00:19:40,773
So much so that I can feel your pain.

217
00:19:41,833 --> 00:19:42,993
But listen to me.

218
00:19:43,273 --> 00:19:47,093
It's ridiculous to lay the blame on a child for the sins of his father.

219
00:19:47,093 --> 00:19:49,753
Did Ace ever do a thing to hurt you?

220
00:19:51,053 --> 00:19:53,793
The two of you have been through so much together.

221
00:19:54,253 --> 00:19:56,093
Some of it happy, some of it painful.

222
00:19:56,493 --> 00:19:58,253
But you've weathered it all.

223
00:19:58,693 --> 00:19:59,973
Good times and bad.

224
00:20:00,233 --> 00:20:01,833
With our brothers in arms.

225
00:20:02,833 --> 00:20:06,733
I never gave a damn about who Ace's father is, and I still don't.

226
00:20:06,733 --> 00:20:10,093
We all crossed paths on these seas by chance.

227
00:20:10,593 --> 00:20:13,853
And wherever the hell we came from doesn't mean a thing anymore.

228
00:20:14,193 --> 00:20:15,593
We're together now.

229
00:20:16,473 --> 00:20:19,053
So, squad, please treat him kindly.

230
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:22,413
I don't love Ace more than any other son of mine.

231
00:20:22,753 --> 00:20:24,333
On that you have my word.

232
00:20:24,833 --> 00:20:27,793
Every single one of you is part of my family.

233
00:20:27,793 --> 00:20:44,053
Now, moving on.

234
00:20:46,553 --> 00:20:47,833
That's Sengoku.

235
00:20:47,833 --> 00:20:54,453
He hasn't changed one bit, the bastard.

236
00:20:54,453 --> 00:20:59,053
But that crafty old snake gave us a pretty good shake-up, didn't he?

237
00:21:00,113 --> 00:21:04,333
But to even suggest that I'd sell out my sons is ridiculous.

238
00:21:17,793 --> 00:21:19,353
They can leave now.

239
00:21:20,233 --> 00:21:21,893
He destroyed the ice wall.

240
00:21:22,293 --> 00:21:23,333
He's a sharp one.

241
00:21:23,333 --> 00:21:31,013
There's nothing blocking our path.

242
00:21:31,713 --> 00:21:32,273
You're right.

243
00:21:32,573 --> 00:21:35,853
We can take these Navy ships and sail away whenever we want.

244
00:21:38,473 --> 00:21:43,693
If you're a true pirate, then you choose which path to take on your own.

245
00:21:43,693 --> 00:21:55,453
I knew it was a lie.

246
00:21:55,833 --> 00:21:57,773
The Navy's just trying to tear us apart.

247
00:21:57,873 --> 00:21:58,713
Come on, guys.

248
00:21:58,813 --> 00:21:59,913
Let's take it to them.

249
00:22:00,013 --> 00:22:01,193
Of course they were lying.

250
00:22:01,273 --> 00:22:03,013
Old Buddy would never betray us.

251
00:22:03,213 --> 00:22:03,813
Hear that?

252
00:22:04,133 --> 00:22:06,913
We'll die before we ever lose trust in you, Old Buddy.

253
00:22:06,913 --> 00:22:08,213
Please forgive me.

254
00:22:08,333 --> 00:22:09,253
We were wrong.

255
00:22:09,393 --> 00:22:12,273
I'll follow you to the end, White Beard, Old Buddy.

256
00:22:12,833 --> 00:22:14,673
Think I'm going soft, do you?

257
00:22:14,673 --> 00:22:16,993
Give it a rest, Crocobum.

258
00:22:17,653 --> 00:22:23,053
I'm only human, and every human has a heart, no matter how large or small.

259
00:22:23,053 --> 00:22:30,193
People can call me a monster all they want, but the reality is I can't be the strongest pirate forever.

260
00:22:30,853 --> 00:22:36,693
If I can save this one young man's life, I'll have earned the right to retire from this world once and for all.

261
00:22:37,733 --> 00:22:41,493
Those of you who will still follow me, put your lives on the line!

262
00:22:41,493 --> 00:22:53,913
It's ready, man!

263
00:22:54,093 --> 00:22:55,293
He's coming his way!

264
00:22:55,753 --> 00:22:58,293
The strongest pirate in the world!

265
00:23:00,993 --> 00:23:02,113
Let's attack!

266
00:23:11,493 --> 00:23:15,893
At last, the world's most powerful pirate, White Beard, leaps into the fray.

267
00:23:16,233 --> 00:23:22,393
The Navy cowers in fear before the power of his Tremor Tremor Fruit, as it literally changes the landscape of the battle.

268
00:23:22,673 --> 00:23:26,073
However, Sengoku has a plan that may yet turn the time.

269
00:23:26,433 --> 00:23:27,973
On the next, One Piece!

270
00:23:28,193 --> 00:23:32,833
The encircling walls activated, the White Beard Pirates backed into a corner.

271
00:23:33,273 --> 00:23:35,093
I'm going to be king of the pirates!

